Z||000000||terry||03-31-2000||10:59 PM||||i love my 84 fiero but i am haveing problems with it. whenever i drive it it drives ok but then when i park it and turn it off then try to restart it it dosnot do anything not even make a sound. then a few hours later i turn the key and bam it cranks. so can someone pleas pleas give me some advice <BR>e mail me at ecktor99@chorus.net ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||03-31-2000||11:10 PM||||check the battery leads, especially the thin ones.<P>check all the leads on the starter. likely the problem is there. make sure none are burnt.<P>could even be the starter over temp.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-01-2000||12:16 AM||||It could be the starter itself too. When they get old they get heat sensitive.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-01-2000||05:26 AM||||I second that! Once the starter gets cooled off it will start when they are old. When they are heated up not even a jump will over come the resistance it gets. Hey, at least you aren't stranded just delayed!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fotofrank||04-01-2000||11:17 AM||||Check the starter for a heat shield.<BR>The solinoid tends to expand and stick when hot,thats why you hear nothing when trying to start a "hot" car. Mine does the same thing but only when the weather is very hot and I drive a long distance.Waiting about 30 - 40 minutes and my '84 starts. Improving the cooling in the engin compartment or wraping the exhaust with heat resistant wrap could help as well as a starter heat shield.||||reg||3
Z||000005||theogre||04-01-2000||05:07 PM||||Check the car for recall compliance. If the recall was done there should be a heat shield on the starter, the firewall, the trunkwall, and a couple other places.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero_86_se||04-02-2000||03:46 AM||||you might have a bad ignition module also.||||reg||1
